.\" groff man page for the Basic Next interpreter executable (0.6 line).
.TH BNI 1 "September 22, 2026" "bni 0.6" "Basic Next"
.SH NAME
bni \- Basic Next checker, interpreter, and editor protocols
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bni
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I source-or-file
.RI [ "-- program-args" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bni
processes UTF-8 Basic Next source through a source-spanned pipeline:
lexer, parser/AST, semantic analysis, typed BN IR, and the reference
interpreter. Compilation is
.BR bnc (1),
which consumes the same validated IR. The 0.5
.B bn
executable is gone:
.B "bn run"
is
.BR "bni run" ,
.B "bn build"
is
.BR bnc .
.PP
The executable module must define
.BR "FUNCTION Start" .
No project file is required for a single program.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B eval
Evaluate one source fragment or complete program through the typed BN IR
interpreter. Pass the source as one argument, or use
.BR --stdin
to consume the complete source from standard input. Arguments after
.B --
are exposed through
.BR HOST.Args .
The
.BR --format
.B json
form emits one JSON v1 result envelope and owns both process channels. This
command is distinct from the file-oriented
.BR run
command.
.TP
.B check
Validate lexical, syntactic, and semantic rules. With
.BR --emit ,
print a selected frontend artifact.
.TP
.B lex
Print the token stream.
.TP
.B run
Validate, lower to typed BN IR, and execute
.BR Start .
The successful process status is the program result.
.TP
.B lsp
Serve the Language Server Protocol over standard input and output.
.TP
.B dap
Serve the Debug Adapter Protocol over standard input and output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Print pipeline stages. Repeat it, or use
.BR -vv ,
to also print tokens.
.TP
.BI --emit " tokens|ast|typed-ast|ir"
Select the frontend artifact printed by
.BR check .
.TP
.BR -o , " --output " file
Write the artifact selected by
.B --emit
to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --mode " snippet|program"
Select
.B eval
fragment or complete-program semantics. The default is
.BR snippet .
.TP
.BI --format " text|json"
Select the
.B eval
result format. JSON emits exactly one versioned envelope on standard output;
it is not available for
.BR check " or " run .
.TP
.BI --module-path " dir"
Append an ordered directory used to resolve imported source modules. The
option is repeatable; earlier directories win. Configuration entries are
applied before command-line entries.
.TP
.B --no-filesystem
With
.BR run ,
reject a
.B HOST.FileSystem
import before
.BR Start .
The Jupyter kernel uses this boundary.
.TP
.B --sandbox
Opt into filesystem root restrictions for
.BR run
(and other commands that honour the sandbox). Without explicit roots, policy
is restrictive; combine with
.B --read-root
and
.BR --write-root .
.TP
.BI --read-root " dir"
Allow reads under
.I dir
when the sandbox is active. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --write-root " dir"
Allow writes under
.I dir
when the sandbox is active. Repeatable.
.TP
.B --trace
Report the interpreter entry point.
.TP
.BI --warnings " errors"
Promote all warning diagnostics to errors.
.TP
.BI --allow " CODE"
Suppress one warning diagnostic (repeatable).
.TP
.BI --warn " CODE"
Keep one warning diagnostic at warning level.
.TP
.BI --deny " CODE"
Promote one warning diagnostic to an error.
.TP
.BI --log-level " error|warn|info|debug"
Process log verbosity (the companion log is written by
.BR bnc (1);
the option is accepted here for a shared configuration).
.TP
.BI --log-file " file"
Companion process log file path (see
.BR bnc (1)).
.TP
.B --no-log
Disable companion process logging.
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Load warning and process logging configuration from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --color " auto|always|never"
Control ANSI colour on status messages.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the tool version.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command help.
.TP
.B --
End tool options. Remaining values become program arguments.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.B HOST.Args
is available only in the executable module and requires no import.
.B HOST.Args[0]
is the absolute source path under
.BR "bni run" ;
later entries are values after
.BR -- .
.B LEN(HOST.Args)
returns the full count.
.PP
.B HOST.Main ,
.BR SYSTEM ,
.BR ArgumentCount() ,
and
.B Argument(index)
were withdrawn in 0.2.
.SH MODULES
Every import declares an alias. Imported declarations are referenced as
.IR alias.member .
User modules belong beneath
.BR modules/ .
Standard modules such as
.BR BNMath ,
.BR BNData ,
.BR BNLog ,
.BR BNWeb ,
and
.B BNJson
belong beneath
.B modules/bn/
and require explicit imports.
.PP
The standard-library directory is located, in order: from
.BR BN_HOME
when set (see ENVIRONMENT); otherwise the nearest
.B modules/bn
above the entry file, then above the working directory, then relative to the
.B bni
executable (installed layout). The effective import roots and the origin of
each one, plus the root that resolved every imported module, are recorded in
the process log at debug level (
.BR "--log-level debug" ).
.PP
.B HOST
is the only built-in interface object. Facilities provided include
.BR HOST.Args ,
.BR HOST.Clock ,
.BR HOST.Console ,
.BR HOST.Random ,
.BR HOST.FileSystem ,
.BR HOST.Net ,
and
.BR HOST.Exec .
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A Basic Next diagnostic exits 1. Invalid command use, missing files, and a
denied execution policy exit 2. Diagnostics include a stable code and source
span when applicable. The interpreter is the reference semantics: a program
that
.BR bnc (1)
rejects as outside the compiler subset still runs here.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BN_HOME
Explicit Basic Next home. When set, the standard-library modules are taken from
.I $BN_HOME/share/bn/modules/bn
or
.IR $BN_HOME/modules/bn ,
and the ancestor-directory search is skipped entirely: a
.B BN_HOME
without a standard library makes standard imports fail rather than silently
resolving to another
.B modules/bn
higher in the tree.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I language/0.6/0.6.ebnf
Accepted grammar for the 0.6 line.
.TP
.I language/0.6/0.6.md
Consolidated 0.6 language specification.
.TP
.I language/0.6/keywords.md
Keyword and reserved-form contract.
.TP
.I docs/project/usage.md
Installation, examples, limits, and troubleshooting.
.TP
.I docs/project/kernel.md
Jupyter host contract.
.TP
.I docs/releases/
In-repo release notes for tagged versions.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Time-zone values do not apply TZDB zone rules.
The VS Code extension and DAP adapter coverage grow with releases; do not assume
full breakpoint/step parity from this page alone.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
bni check examples/hello.bn
bni eval 'PRINT 1 + 1'
printf 'PRINT 2\n' | bni eval --stdin
bni run examples/language-tour.bn
bni run examples/hello.bn -- extra-argument
bni check --emit ir examples/factorial.bn
bni run --sandbox --read-root . --write-root /tmp examples/hello.bn
.RE
.fi
